      "description": "Watch Crawley Town vs Crewe highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The League Two clash on 2026-08-15 between Crawley Town and Crewe was a game that prioritized grit and disciplinary drama over free-flowing football. Fans at the stadium witnessed an afternoon where the referee's notebook was as busy as the players on the pitch. Red Card Chaos Disrupts Momentum The first half served as a precursor to the chaos, with yellow cards handed out to Jordan Gibson and Jude Arthurs as both teams struggled to find a clinical edge. However, the game truly ignited in the second half. In the 51st minute, Crawley Town were dealt a massive blow when Kellan Gordon was shown a straight red card. The decision sparked heavy protests from his teammates, but the official remained unmoved. Things went from bad to worse for the home side just fifteen minutes later. In the 65th minute, Malcolm Ebiowei became the second Crawley player to be sent off with a straight red card. Facing a two-man disadvantage, the hosts were forced into a desperate defensive shell, making multiple tactical substitutions to try and preserve a point. March Steals the Victory Crewe looked to capitalize on their numerical superiority, but they too suffered a disciplinary setback when Mickey Demetriou received a second yellow card and was sent off in the 85th minute. Despite the game moving to a 10-on-9 scenario, the pressure from the visitors remained constant as the clock ticked into twelve minutes of stoppage time. The deadlock was finally broken in the 95th minute. Joel Tabiner provided a pinpoint assist for Josh March , who stayed composed to slot the ball home and make it 0-1 . It was a clinical finish that decided a fractious encounter, leaving the home supporters frustrated after a resilient but ill-disciplined performance."
